  "id": "atypical-depression",
  "term": "atypical depression",
  "definition": "Atypical depression is a form of depression in which mood can improve in response to positive events, alongside features such as increased appetite, oversleeping, heavy feelings in the limbs, and long-term sensitivity to rejection from others. It is also often seen together with weight gain and other metabolic and inflammatory changes.",
